-- ============================================================
-- Marksmanship: Concussive Barrage
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Your Multi Shot has a 50/100% chance to reduce the channeled
--  duration of the next Volley by 2.5 secs, reduce the mana cost by 100%, and
--  shote fire every .5 secs.  (2 ranks) (Arcane Barrage, the arcane mage spell,
--  for Volley)"
--
-- Entirely DBC, and barely even new: Missile Barrage (44401) is this exact
-- design already -- three spellmods on one aura, MiscValue 1 (DURATION),
-- 19 (ACTIVATION_TIME) and 14 (COST), base points -2501 / -501 / -101, 15s
-- duration.  200758 is a straight clone with SpellFamilyName 9 and every class
-- mask moved from Arcane Missiles (2048) to Volley (8192).
--
-- Why those three effects work, verified rather than assumed:
--
--   * DURATION reaches a CHANNEL.  Spell::handle_immediate (Spell.cpp:4074-4092)
--     applies SPELLMOD_DURATION before haste and before SendChannelStart.  Its
--     own comment cites Missile Barrage.  Volley gets there despite Speed 30.0
--     because Spell::cast only defers when Speed > 0 && !IsChanneled()
--     (Spell.cpp:3941).
--   * ACTIVATION_TIME reaches the tick rate.  AuraEffect::CalculatePeriodic
--     (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:646) applies it under GetId() -- Volley's own id --
--     so the class mask matches directly.  FLAT only; PCT does nothing here.
--   * One charge, not three.  Player::RemoveSpellMods erases the aura from
--     m_appliedMods before dropping the charge (Player.cpp:10062), with a
--     comment saying exactly why.
--
-- Net effect: 6000ms channel -> 3500ms, 1000ms ticks -> 500ms, so SEVEN ticks
-- where there were six.  That is a ~17% damage increase on top of the free
-- cast, not merely a convenience -- if Volley proves too strong, retune Volley's
-- tick damage rather than this buff.
--
-- Expect the buff icon to linger visibly for the whole channel: for a channeled
-- spell the charge drops at Spell::finish (Spell.cpp:4523), i.e. at channel
-- END, not at channel start.  Cosmetic only.



